.SH NAME
mygrep \- find lines containing a search string

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <stdio.h>
.br
.B int mygrep(FILE *fp, const char *search_str, char ***matches);

.SH DESCRIPTION
The mygrep() function reads a file line by line and finds
the lines that contain the specified search string.

The matching lines are stored in dynamically allocated memory
and returned through the matches parameter.

.SH RETURN VALUE
The function returns the number of matching lines.
It returns -1 if an invalid argument is provided or memory
allocation fails.

